 Most warlocks in classic WoW use voidwalkers for their superior tanking abilities, particularly the taunt and threat generation from Torment and Suffering, which help keep mobs off the warlock. While succubus offers better single-target damage and crowd control, the voidwalker's ability to hold aggro and reduce downtime with Consume Shadows makes it a more reliable choice for general leveling and questing. [end of text]


